            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Paul Dirac</strong><br>\nPaul Dirac was born in 1902 in Bristol, England. His father was Swiss and his mother was English. He was an excellent student, especially in mathematics. From a young age, Dirac was known for his precise and clear thinking, which later helped him in his scientific career. He studied electrical engineering at the University of Bristol before switching to mathematics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Transition to Theoretical Physics</strong><br>\nAfter completing his engineering degree, Dirac's interest shifted to theoretical physics. He received a scholarship to study at the University of Cambridge, where he began to work on the general theory of relativity and quantum mechanics. His studies led him to earn a PhD under the supervision of the famous atomic theorist Ralph Fowler.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Quantum Mechanics and the Dirac Equation</strong><br>\nDirac's work on quantum mechanics revolutionized the field. In 1928, he derived the Dirac equation, which combined quantum mechanics and special relativity. This equation predicted the existence of antimatter, a previously unknown concept that was later confirmed by experiments. His equation also provided a deeper understanding of the electron's spin.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
